WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.230
Use Form Mode when you know the issue and want to enter it field by field.

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:08.620
Start in AI Assistant, then switch to Form Mode before typing.

00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:11.680
Write a title that names the equipment and the failure.

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:16.030
Headset microphone cuts out is more useful in a queue than please help.

00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:19.720
In the description, separate observation from diagnosis.

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:25.980
Record which unit failed, the movement that caused the sound to drop, and the spare used to keep class running.

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:29.500
Do not call the cable defective unless someone has verified it.

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:30.620
Choose Next.

00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:35.230
Under Repair and Maintenance, pick Audio, Mic and Headphone Malfunction.

00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:38.750
Read the suggested priority in light of the actual disruption.

00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:44.600
On the location step, select the studio where the equipment failed, not the office filing the report.

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:46.850
Work through the people and detail steps.

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:50.680
Do not invent an instructor or a member to fill an optional field.

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:56.080
At Review and Submit, compare the title, category and studio with your original report.

00:00:56.080 --> 00:00:59.420
If anything disagrees, go back before creating the ticket.

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:01.370
Select Create Ticket once.

00:01:01.370 --> 00:01:05.880
In All Tickets, open the new row, note the ticket number, and reload.

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:09.430
The same number and title are your evidence that the report was saved.
